br.br:
1.    (Currently Amended) A wearable fetal health monitoring device for determining a heath condition of a fetus based on biosignals of an expecting mother and the fetus, the device comprising:a microelectromechanical system (MEMS) accelerometer that converts an acoustic wave sensed in an abdominal region into an abdominal acoustic signal;

a pulse oximeter that generates a maternal photoplethysmogram (mPPG) value from a pulse sensed in the abdominal region;

a ferroelectric nanogenerator sensor that detects abdominal pressure waves;and

a microcontroller configured to:

generate a maternal phonocardiogram (mPCG) value from the abdominal acoustic signal;

calculate a first maternal heart rate (mHR) value from the mPCG value;

calculate a second mHR value from the mPPG value;

compare the first mHR value with the second mHR value to identify a noise correction value; and

apply the identified noise correction value to the mPCG value to extract a fetal phonocardiogram (fPCG) value.



2.    (Original) The device of claim 1, further comprising at least one of: a power source operatively coupled to a wireless transceiver, a memory, and an electrode.





3.    (Original) The device of claim 1, wherein the microcontroller is further configured to calculate from the fPCG value at least one of: a fetal heart rate (fHR) value and a fetal heart rate variability (fHRV) value.

4.
(Original) The device of claim 1, wherein the microcontroller is further configured to calculate a fetal movement (fM) value from the abdominal acoustic signal.

5.
(Original) The device of claim 1, wherein the pulse oximeter is further configured to sense a maternal peripheral capillary oxygen saturation (mSpO2) value.



6.    (Original) The device of claim 1, wherein the MEMS accelerometer comprises at least one of an acoustic wave sensor and a pressure wave sensor.

7.
(Original) The device of claim 1, wherein the microcontroller is further configured to calculate a maternal activity level from at least one of the mPPG value and the first mHR value and the second mHR value.



8.    (Original) The device of claim 1, further comprising one or more of: a MEMS inclinometer, an inertia sensor, and a gyroscope.

9.
(Currently Amended) The device of claim 1, further comprising a patch configured to removably attach that removably attaches to a maternal torso.



10.   (Original) The device of claim 1, wherein the device comprises two units spaced apart from each other, wherein the two units are carried on a belt or band that surrounds a maternal torso.



11.   (Original) The device of claim 1, wherein the device further comprises an acoustic impedance matching housing.





12.   (Original) The device of claim 1, wherein the microcontroller is further configured to deconvolute the abdominal acoustic signal using at least one of the first mHR value and the second mHR value.



13.   (Original) The device of claim 1, further comprising an inclinometer sensor that detects a sub-audible abdominal acoustic wave.



14.   (Original) The device of claim 1, wherein a first portion of the device is disposable, and wherein a second portion of the device is re-usable.



15.   (Canceled)



16.   (Original) The device of claim 1, further comprising a noise attenuator configured to: at least partially constructively or destructively combine a first physiological signal component of a first signal output by a first acoustic sensor and a second physiological signal component of a second signal output by a second acoustic sensor.



17.   (Currently Amended) A method of determining a heath condition of a fetus based on biosignals of an expecting mother and the fetus, the method comprising:providing a wearable fetal health monitoring device, comprising:

a microelectromechanical system (MEMS) accelerometer that converts an acoustic wave sensed in an abdominal region into an abdominal acoustic signal;

a pulse oximeter that generates a maternal photoplethysmogram (mPPG) value from a pulse sensed in the abdominal region;

a ferroelectric nanogenerator sensor that detects abdominal pressure waves;and

a microcontroller configured to:



generate a maternal phonocardiogram (mPCG) value from the abdominal acoustic signal;

calculate a first maternal heart rate (mHR) value from the mPCG value;

calculate a second mHR value from the mPPG value;

compare the first mHR value with the second mHR value to identify a noise correction value; and

apply the identified noise correction value to the mPCG value to extract a fetal phonocardiogram (fPCG) value.

generating a maternal phonocardiogram (mPCG) value from the abdominal acoustic signal;

calculating a first maternal heart rate (mHR) value from the mPCG value;

calculating a second mHR value from the mPPG value;

comparing the first mHR value with the second mHR value to identify a noise correction value;

applying the identified noise correction value to the mPCG value to extract a fetal phonocardiogram (fPCG) value.



18.   (Original) The method of claim 17, further comprising calculating from the fPCG value at least one of: a fetal heart rate (fHR) value and a fetal heart rate variability (fHRV) value.



19.   (Original) The method of claim 17, further comprising outputting at least one of a normal state, caution state, and emergency state based on the extracted fetal phonocardiogram (fPCG) value.



20.   (Original) The method of claim 17, further comprising calculating a fetal movement (fM) value from the abdominal acoustic signal.





21.   (New) A non-transitory computer-readable storage medium, the non-transitory computer-readable storage medium storing instructions to be implemented on a wearable fetal health monitoring device comprising:a microelectromechanical system (MEMS) accelerometer that converts an acoustic wave sensed in an abdominal region into an abdominal acoustic signal;

a pulse oximeter that generates a maternal photoplethysmogram (mPPG) value from a pulse sensed in the abdominal region;

a ferroelectric nanogenerator sensor that detects abdominal pressure waves; and

at least one processor;

the instructions when executed by the at least one processor cause wearable fetal health monitoring device to perform a method of determining a heath condition of a fetus based on biosignals of an expecting mother and the fetus, the method comprising:generating a maternal phonocardiogram (mPCG) value from the abdominal acoustic signal;

calculating a first maternal heart rate (mHR) value from the mPCG value;

calculating a second mHR value from the mPPG value;

comparing the first mHR value with the second mHR value to identify a noise correction value; and

applying the identified noise correction value to the mPCG value to extract a fetal phonocardiogram (fPCG) value.
